{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T2-002", "approach": "LEX6", "approach_base": "LEX6", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "Douglass learned to read in Baltimore when Mrs. Auld kindly began teaching him the A, B, C and helped him spell words of three or four letters (Chapter VI). Mr. Auld then forbade her to continue, saying it was unlawful as well as unsafe to teach a slave to read (Chapter VI). He argued that learning would spoil a slave, make him unmanageable, and \"forever unfit him to be a slave\" (Chapter VI). Douglass finished learning to read and write with the assistance of his master's wife, as noted in the biographical introduction (Frederick Douglass).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 1011 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o011", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b109", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b110"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [76319, 77330], "meta": {"chunk": 5734, "completed": 14, "prefix": 0, "provenance": [["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", 76319, 77330, "body"]]}}, {"text": "[stripped: 650 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o015", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b197", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b198"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [173593, 174243], "meta": {"chunk": 5877, "completed": 39, "prefix": 0, "provenance": [["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", 173593, 174243, "body"]]}}, {"text": "[stripped: 886 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o005", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b50"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [25277,