{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T3-001", "approach": "LEX6", "approach_base": "LEX6", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "The material is tallow, which comes from suet—the fat of the ox (Russian tallow, per Faraday's lecture). It was converted into the beautiful substance stearin by Gay Lussac, or someone entrusted with his knowledge, as described in the candle lecture section \"A CANDLE: THE FLAME—ITS SOURCES—STRUCTURE—MOBILITY—BRIGHTNESS.\" Faraday notes that stearin candles are clean rather than greasy like ordinary tallow candles.", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 885 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::o029", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::p1_b42"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [6871, 7756], "meta": {"chunk": 2542, "completed": 55, "prefix": 0, "provenance": [["K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en", 6871, 7756, "body"]]}}, {"text": "[stripped: 892 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::o029", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::p1_b47", "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::p1_b48"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [15931, 16823], "meta": {"chunk": 2555, "completed": 9, "prefix": 0, "provenance": [["K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en", 15931, 16823, "body"]]}}, {"text": "[stripped: 1009 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::o029", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-14474_faraday_chemical-history-of-a-candle.en::p1_b41", "K.